    rdf:value """Tuesday Oct. 18.98. Frullino. Florence
Had a singing lesson. Chatted in the evening. 
Wednesday Oct. 19.98 
A quiet day of work. Miss Hamilton called on Bernhard, whom she insisted on calling “Professor Berenson”. Bernhard and Alys and Bertie called on the Benns.
Thursday Oct. 20.98, 
Music lesson – haven’t lost so much as I feared. Shopped with Alys. Read Goethe in the evening. 
Friday Oct. 21.98 
Miss Lowndes to lunch – dull and rather depressing. Alys and I drove to Settignano, but Mr. Power was out, so we had a chat with Mr. Price, who is recovering from having the first joint of his finger  bitten off  by a savage gardener. Then we drove to Careggi to see Mrs. Scott-Barber, Bertie and """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 84 ;
